1
00:01:31,972 --> 00:01:33,662
Step right up, step right up!

2
00:01:33,756 --> 00:01:36,456
Delicious candy that tastes sweet
no matter where you lick it!

3
00:01:36,754 --> 00:01:38,785
A candy that never runs out,
no matter how long you lick it!

4
00:01:38,905 --> 00:01:40,541
Hey there, step right up!

5
00:01:40,565 --> 00:01:43,056
Hey there, step right up, step right up!
Sold, sold, sold!

6
00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:44,431
Delicious, so delicious, delicious candy!

7
00:01:44,455 --> 00:01:48,231
Thanks a lot, thanks a lot, thanks a lot!

8
00:01:48,276 --> 00:01:51,088
Hey tasty, isn't it? 
Sweet and delicious candy.

9
00:01:51,236 --> 00:01:53,236
It's a candy that never runs out!

10
00:01:53,261 --> 00:01:56,244
No, no, no! Come on,
keep licking, faster and faster!

11
00:01:56,307 --> 00:01:58,830
Must be nice... Must be real nice.

12
00:01:58,994 --> 00:02:01,986
It's delicious! Ah, keep on licking!

13
00:02:02,666 --> 00:02:04,119
Come again!

14
00:02:11,466 --> 00:02:12,438
Wait!

15
00:02:16,938 --> 00:02:18,514
You think I'll let you get away?!

16
00:02:25,044 --> 00:02:27,720
What the hell? You ruined my candy!

17
00:02:30,582 --> 00:02:32,939
I saw you! You're a thief!

18
00:02:32,964 --> 00:02:35,214
Shut up, you brat!

19
00:02:37,394 --> 00:02:39,420
I'm an oak tree puppet!

20
00:02:39,670 --> 00:02:41,480
Bruno, what are you doing?

21
00:02:41,634 --> 00:02:43,425
Oh, Papa!

22
00:02:52,423 --> 00:02:54,583
He called me a thief!

23
00:02:55,010 --> 00:02:57,380
I saw you steal that candy!

24
00:02:59,774 --> 00:03:02,840
The one who gets robbed is the real fool.

25
00:03:03,473 --> 00:03:06,940
B-But stealing from other people is wrong!

26
00:03:08,739 --> 00:03:10,980
You say you're an oak tree puppet?

27
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:17,220
A talking puppet? Now that's 
something you don't see every day.

28
00:03:19,740 --> 00:03:21,240
Who made you?

29
00:03:21,429 --> 00:03:22,620
Grandpa did.

30
00:03:23,524 --> 00:03:24,524
Grandpa?

31
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:37,260
Ah, do you really want to 
become a human that badly?

32
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:41,760
Of course I do! I want to eat chocolate
and candy just like everyone else.

33
00:03:44,829 --> 00:03:45,638
Delicious!

34
00:03:47,780 --> 00:03:50,505
By the way, what are you guys
doing in a place like this?

35
00:03:50,785 --> 00:03:52,120
Earning a living.

36
00:03:52,384 --> 00:03:53,384
Doing what?

37
00:03:57,154 --> 00:03:58,740
Look, they're back.

38
00:04:00,706 --> 00:04:03,016
Boss, here's today's take.

39
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:04,580
Here, hand it over.

40
00:04:06,219 --> 00:04:08,900
Yeah, not bad. You guys can eat, too.

41
00:04:10,441 --> 00:04:16,300
We tried to kidnap some kids, but they're
pretty cautious and wouldn't come near us.

42
00:04:16,325 --> 00:04:18,959
Damn kids are getting too smart these days.

43
00:04:19,620 --> 00:04:21,899
Oh, are you guys gypsies?

44
00:04:22,880 --> 00:04:26,263
That's right. When we find a 
foolish kid, we snatch them up...

45
00:04:26,287 --> 00:04:29,180
...and sell them cheap to 
anyone who wants one.

46
00:04:29,540 --> 00:04:31,340
I-I-I'm going home!

47
00:04:31,780 --> 00:04:32,780
Hold on!

48
00:04:34,580 --> 00:04:37,350
Don't worry, we're not gonna kidnap you.

49
00:04:37,780 --> 00:04:40,700
There's no point in 
kidnapping a wooden puppet.

50
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:42,420
You said your name was Mokku, right?

51
00:04:43,610 --> 00:04:45,660
How'd you like me to turn you into a human?

52
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:49,800
With this magic ring.

53
00:04:51,225 --> 00:04:54,629
I've never cast magic on a 
wooden puppet with this before.

54
00:04:54,653 --> 00:04:57,057
It only works on lazy people, after all.

55
00:04:57,082 --> 00:04:59,430
I don't really like working much.

56
00:04:59,510 --> 00:05:01,440
No, let's try casting it.

57
00:05:02,715 --> 00:05:04,720
Do as I say...

58
00:05:07,180 --> 00:05:08,920
This and that...

59
00:05:13,820 --> 00:05:15,560
Village, museum...

60
00:05:37,060 --> 00:05:38,320
Pinch yourself.

61
00:05:38,580 --> 00:05:39,220
Huh?

62
00:05:41,300 --> 00:05:42,000
Ow!

63
00:05:42,295 --> 00:05:44,040
It really hurts!

64
00:05:44,365 --> 00:05:46,900
It worked. Now eat this.

65
00:05:52,310 --> 00:05:55,365
It's delicious! Is meat really this good?

66
00:06:07,663 --> 00:06:09,580
Suddenly it doesn't taste good anymore.

67
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:13,660
You turned back into a wooden puppet.

68
00:06:14,500 --> 00:06:17,623
Please, Boss! Make me human again!

69
00:06:18,824 --> 00:06:21,995
I'll be your servant, I'll do 
anything! Please, Boss!

70
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:25,503
Only if you bring me a hundred gold coins.

71
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:27,496
I don't have that kind of money!

72
00:06:28,180 --> 00:06:31,120
Then bring me the old bastard who made you.

73
00:06:31,565 --> 00:06:32,732
Grandpa?

74
00:06:33,055 --> 00:06:36,220
That's right. Do that, and 
I'll make you human.

75
00:06:36,244 --> 00:06:37,340
Grandpa?

76
00:06:49,090 --> 00:06:51,340
Mokku, do you want something?

77
00:06:52,750 --> 00:06:53,960
G-Grandpa?

78
00:06:54,740 --> 00:06:56,393
Mokku, what is the matter?

79
00:06:57,630 --> 00:06:59,620
I want to become human, no matter what!

80
00:07:00,910 --> 00:07:04,731
A Gypsy in the forest cast a spell 
on me earlier, and I became human!

81
00:07:05,710 --> 00:07:09,620
That's ridiculous! 
Magic can't turn you into a human!

82
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:14,615
It's true! It hurt when I pinched myself, 
and I even got to eat meat!

83
00:07:14,846 --> 00:07:15,436
But...

84
00:07:16,546 --> 00:07:20,276
...the wizard said he won't 
cast any more magic...

85
00:07:20,777 --> 00:07:23,540
...unless I bring a hundred gold coins 
or bring Grandpa to him.

86
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:26,823
But I could never do that.

87
00:07:26,847 --> 00:07:31,000
Grandpa is too precious to me.

88
00:07:33,380 --> 00:07:36,829
Still... I really want to 
eat meat like that again.

89
00:07:39,970 --> 00:07:42,820
If it's what you wish for,
I'll do anything.

90
00:07:42,970 --> 00:07:45,674
Really? Really? Truly?

91
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:49,400
Yes, truly. Come here.

92
00:07:50,580 --> 00:07:52,065
Grandpa!

93
00:07:52,775 --> 00:07:57,048
It's all right, it's all right. 
In return, you must be a good boy.

94
00:08:05,550 --> 00:08:10,705
I'll work hard and save up a hundred
gold coins real fast, and come get you!

95
00:08:11,490 --> 00:08:14,658
Make sure you sleep 
under a blanket at night.

96
00:08:14,682 --> 00:08:18,961
If you're ever in trouble, go ask 
your teacher or the priest for help.

97
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:20,099
Okay.

98
00:08:20,910 --> 00:08:23,048
All right, old man, time to go.

99
00:08:23,715 --> 00:08:25,193
Mokku, take care of yourself.

100
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:28,211
You take care too, Grandpa!

101
00:08:29,189 --> 00:08:30,510
Yes, yes.

102
00:08:32,065 --> 00:08:33,589
Hyah!

103
00:08:42,709 --> 00:08:45,533
Grandpa! Goodbye!

104
00:08:53,959 --> 00:08:55,369
He's gone...

105
00:08:57,252 --> 00:08:58,025
♪ Itai! ♪
It hurts!

106
00:08:58,674 --> 00:09:01,260
♪ Itai! Itai! Itai! Itai! ♪
It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts!

107
00:09:01,638 --> 00:09:02,820
♪ Itainda! ♪
It hurts!

108
00:09:05,843 --> 00:09:07,134
♪ Itainda! ♪
It hurts!

109
00:09:07,182 --> 00:09:08,499
♪ Itai yo! ♪
It hurts!

110
00:09:08,579 --> 00:09:09,897
♪ Itai na! ♪
It hurts!

111
00:09:10,033 --> 00:09:12,549
♪ A-! Ita ta to ta-! ♪
Ah! Ow, ow... ow...

112
00:09:12,784 --> 00:09:15,460
♪ Itai yo~. Itai na~. ♪
It hurts~. It hurts~.

113
00:09:15,549 --> 00:09:18,096
♪ Ita ta no ta no ta no ta ♪
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

114
00:09:18,151 --> 00:09:19,830
♪ Haitta koto... ♪
It actually hurts...

115
00:09:22,109 --> 00:09:25,039
I'm a human now. I can eat anything!

116
00:09:25,470 --> 00:09:27,649
Now, where's something to eat...?

117
00:09:33,290 --> 00:09:34,420
Time to eat!

118
00:09:37,201 --> 00:09:41,420
Gross... Did Grandpa really 
eat stuff this awful...?

119
00:09:43,858 --> 00:09:46,419
Hey, Mokku! What have you done?

120
00:09:46,693 --> 00:09:48,304
You sold Grandfather, didn't you?!

121
00:09:49,989 --> 00:09:52,259
Grandpa said he wanted to go himself!

122
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:53,443
You ungrateful brat!

123
00:09:53,584 --> 00:09:57,847
Do you really think you can survive on your
own without Grandfather? Well, Mokku?!

124
00:09:58,052 --> 00:10:01,920
Shut up! I'm the master of this 
house now! Get out! Get out!

125
00:10:01,921 --> 00:10:05,299
It's not too late! Go and bring 
Grandfather back right now!

126
00:10:06,583 --> 00:10:08,270
Mind your own business! Get out!

127
00:10:08,715 --> 00:10:10,902
You can't even fry an egg!

128
00:10:11,277 --> 00:10:13,590
You'll starve and end up a beggar!

129
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:17,078
Beggar or not, who cares as long as 
I get to eat delicious food?!

130
00:10:17,271 --> 00:10:18,271
You busybody!

131
00:10:19,620 --> 00:10:21,752
Right, it still hurts...

132
00:10:22,737 --> 00:10:25,580
Good grief, don't come crying to me 
when everything goes wrong!

133
00:10:29,076 --> 00:10:30,215
What are you talking about?

134
00:10:30,568 --> 00:10:32,340
The fun is just getting started.

135
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:39,798
Grandpa isn't here and I'm really hungry.

136
00:10:39,822 --> 00:10:41,764
Please, can I just have one piece of candy?

137
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:47,220
What? The only people entitled to 
charity are the elderly and the sick.

138
00:10:47,392 --> 00:10:49,420
If you want candy, go earn it.

139
00:10:50,075 --> 00:10:52,120
But I'm just a kid!

140
00:10:52,874 --> 00:10:55,794
Even a kid can do some simple chores.

141
00:10:56,105 --> 00:10:58,660
Help me out with my work,
and I'll give you some candy.

142
00:10:58,860 --> 00:11:02,269
You're just saying that so you can 
make me work for free, mister!

143
00:11:02,455 --> 00:11:03,520
No way!

144
00:11:03,600 --> 00:11:07,880
Then suit yourself! It serves a lazy 
brat like you right to go hungry!

145
00:11:09,029 --> 00:11:11,421
Cheapskate! You're just stingy!

146
00:11:11,500 --> 00:11:12,109
What?!

147
00:11:16,399 --> 00:11:18,969
What a rotten kid, 
when you're the one who's lazy!

148
00:11:26,769 --> 00:11:28,790
Being human is so lame.

149
00:11:28,939 --> 00:11:31,468
You can't eat anything unless you work.

150
00:11:40,004 --> 00:11:42,164
I'm never going to work.

151
00:11:43,499 --> 00:11:46,020
Mokku, haven't you learned your lesson yet?

152
00:11:49,818 --> 00:11:51,299
W-What's wrong, Mokku?

153
00:11:55,409 --> 00:11:56,999
Stop! Those are poisonous berries!

154
00:11:57,140 --> 00:11:57,804
Shut up!

155
00:11:58,670 --> 00:12:00,098
Stop! They'll kill you!

156
00:12:00,712 --> 00:12:03,185
Mokku! Those are poison! Stop!

157
00:12:14,210 --> 00:12:16,920
It hurts! My stomach hurts!

158
00:12:18,019 --> 00:12:19,320
Ah, finally!

159
00:12:19,345 --> 00:12:21,540
It hurts! It hurts! It hurts so much!

160
00:12:23,329 --> 00:12:25,440
I told you so!

161
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:28,520
It hurts!

162
00:12:31,709 --> 00:12:34,360
It hurts! It hurts! It hurts!

163
00:12:37,426 --> 00:12:39,245
Mokku, are you all right?

164
00:12:40,599 --> 00:12:43,940
I don't want to be human anymore! 
I hate being human!

165
00:12:44,929 --> 00:12:48,620
Mokku, you have not become a real human.

166
00:12:50,039 --> 00:12:51,900
You cannot become human just yet.

167
00:12:52,445 --> 00:12:53,445
Why not?

168
00:12:54,319 --> 00:12:57,460
Because you do not possess a 
righteous and kind heart.

169
00:12:57,915 --> 00:13:00,201
But I don't want to become human anymore!

170
00:13:00,748 --> 00:13:02,460
Nothing good ever comes of it!

171
00:13:03,300 --> 00:13:06,620
That is because you do not 
yet know true joy.

172
00:13:07,420 --> 00:13:08,740
True joy?

173
00:13:09,100 --> 00:13:11,435
Humans have many kinds of joy.

174
00:13:11,460 --> 00:13:12,951
The joy of living...

175
00:13:13,358 --> 00:13:14,615
...the joy of loving...

176
00:13:15,866 --> 00:13:17,065
...the joy of working.

177
00:13:17,860 --> 00:13:19,862
Is working really that fun?

178
00:13:20,229 --> 00:13:20,826
Yes.

179
00:13:21,405 --> 00:13:24,040
But only those who sweat with 
their own effort can understand it.

180
00:13:24,215 --> 00:13:26,340
Then what should I do?

181
00:13:27,172 --> 00:13:29,123
If you turn the wizard's 
ring the other way...

182
00:13:29,483 --> 00:13:31,427
...you can return to being
an Oak Tree puppet.

183
00:13:32,320 --> 00:13:36,280
And then, you must strive to 
have a righteous and kind heart.

184
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:38,160
Do you understand?

185
00:13:42,041 --> 00:13:43,041
Ah, wait!

186
00:13:48,689 --> 00:13:49,940
She's gone...

187
00:13:52,135 --> 00:13:54,618
All right! I'll do it! 
I'll definitely do it!

188
00:13:54,759 --> 00:13:56,433
That's it! That's the spirit!

189
00:13:57,369 --> 00:13:58,369
Wh-Who are you?

190
00:13:59,759 --> 00:14:01,700
I'm Giorgio the crow.

191
00:14:02,060 --> 00:14:02,680
Giorgio?

192
00:14:02,860 --> 00:14:04,160
Look what showed up.

193
00:14:05,030 --> 00:14:07,090
The Oak Tree Fairy sent me.

194
00:14:07,251 --> 00:14:09,502
You're an enchanted devil, after all.

195
00:14:09,526 --> 00:14:11,380
The moment I look away, 
you get into mischief.

196
00:14:11,645 --> 00:14:16,260
My family's been nesting in that Oak Tree 
for generations, you know.

197
00:14:16,670 --> 00:14:18,320
So I couldn't say no.

198
00:14:18,445 --> 00:14:20,973
Hmph! I don't need someone 
like you here anyway!

199
00:14:21,200 --> 00:14:22,900
I'm not a devil!

200
00:14:23,761 --> 00:14:27,198
The proof that you're a devil is that
you have no empathy for others.

201
00:14:27,397 --> 00:14:29,697
When you act like that, take this!

202
00:14:31,660 --> 00:14:32,660
Serves you right.

203
00:14:33,460 --> 00:14:37,598
Listen, Mokku. If you get any bad ideas
from now on, I won't hesitate to peck you.

204
00:14:38,105 --> 00:14:39,602
That's so mean!

205
00:14:40,760 --> 00:14:45,786
This is great. I think I'll leave things to 
Giorgio the crow for a bit and take a rest.

206
00:15:02,613 --> 00:15:04,520
All right, here is the wizard's house.

207
00:15:04,945 --> 00:15:06,428
It looks kind of scary...

208
00:15:06,452 --> 00:15:08,946
Are you whining again?

209
00:15:09,999 --> 00:15:10,891
Ouch!

210
00:15:11,070 --> 00:15:12,460
Here I go!

211
00:15:18,250 --> 00:15:20,380
Oh, they look just like me.

212
00:15:22,249 --> 00:15:24,760
And they're all a bit strange.

213
00:15:26,959 --> 00:15:28,128
What did you come here for?!

214
00:15:35,539 --> 00:15:36,939
What do you want?!

215
00:15:37,739 --> 00:15:42,485
Please give Grandpa back! And please 
turn me back into a wooden puppet!

216
00:15:42,825 --> 00:15:45,024
Did you bring the 100 gold coins?

217
00:15:46,209 --> 00:15:50,185
But I didn't want to be a devil! 
I wanted to be human!

218
00:15:50,820 --> 00:15:51,899
What did you say?

219
00:15:52,299 --> 00:15:54,371
I never asked to be made into a devil!

220
00:15:54,716 --> 00:15:56,860
Now give me back my Grandpa!

221
00:15:57,280 --> 00:15:58,280
Shut your mouth!

222
00:15:58,615 --> 00:15:59,615
Let go of me!

223
00:16:00,180 --> 00:16:01,395
Cheeky little brat.

224
00:16:01,795 --> 00:16:04,740
Bruno, take him to the old man 
and make him help out!

225
00:16:05,588 --> 00:16:08,176
Make them churn out defective puppets!

226
00:16:10,648 --> 00:16:11,648
Move it!

227
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:23,640
Mokku!

228
00:16:23,851 --> 00:16:24,680
Grandpa!

229
00:16:25,380 --> 00:16:28,425
Old man, Mokku is your assistant now.
Work him to the bone!

230
00:16:28,820 --> 00:16:29,820
Mokku!

231
00:16:29,860 --> 00:16:31,860
Grandpa, I'm so sorry...

232
00:16:32,575 --> 00:16:36,820
I missed you. I was 
worried sick about you...

233
00:16:38,429 --> 00:16:40,975
Grandpa, they turned me into a devil...

234
00:16:40,999 --> 00:16:42,529
Is that so?

235
00:16:42,553 --> 00:16:46,858
I've been locked up here as well,
forced to do this awful work.

236
00:16:47,296 --> 00:16:48,579
What are we going to do?

237
00:16:49,040 --> 00:16:52,069
There's nothing an old man 
like me can do...

238
00:16:52,233 --> 00:16:54,643
I never should have come here...

239
00:16:55,835 --> 00:16:56,393
Ouch!

240
00:16:56,589 --> 00:16:58,014
What's the matter?

241
00:16:58,218 --> 00:17:00,038
Mokku, so it really hurts?

242
00:17:00,686 --> 00:17:01,850
I get it now.

243
00:17:03,647 --> 00:17:05,480
Don't worry, Grandpa. 
I'll definitely save you!

244
00:17:05,679 --> 00:17:07,512
And then I'll turn back
into a normal puppet!

245
00:17:20,297 --> 00:17:21,040
Now!

246
00:17:23,379 --> 00:17:24,099
Do it right!

247
00:17:30,519 --> 00:17:33,860
If I turn that ring backward, 
I can turn back into a puppet!

248
00:18:13,551 --> 00:18:14,700
This will do it!

249
00:18:15,524 --> 00:18:16,524
I did it!

250
00:18:16,814 --> 00:18:18,335
All right, pinch me!

251
00:18:19,540 --> 00:18:20,540
It doesn't hurt, does it?

252
00:18:20,905 --> 00:18:22,200
Now I'm back to being a puppet!

253
00:18:22,537 --> 00:18:23,420
Hurray!

254
00:18:28,289 --> 00:18:32,140
Thank goodness, thank goodness, Mokku. 
But I'm staying here.

255
00:18:32,284 --> 00:18:34,140
Why? Why, Grandpa?

256
00:18:34,484 --> 00:18:38,561
I was the one who made those 
defective puppets. I can't just run away.

257
00:18:38,671 --> 00:18:42,420
But if you stay here, they'll just force 
you to make more defective puppets!

258
00:18:43,164 --> 00:18:47,880
I will never make puppets like that again. 
Now, go back to the village on your own.

259
00:18:48,839 --> 00:18:51,060
If you're not going, 
Grandpa, I'm staying too.

260
00:18:51,469 --> 00:18:55,180
You can't do that. If you stay in a place
like this, they'll put a spell on you again.

261
00:18:55,594 --> 00:18:57,720
I can't go back and
leave you behind, Grandpa!

262
00:18:59,154 --> 00:18:59,897
Mokku...

263
00:18:59,921 --> 00:19:03,370
I know I'm a bad boy, 
but I love you most of all, Grandpa.

264
00:19:04,205 --> 00:19:08,181
- Mokku... Mokku...
- Grandpa.

265
00:19:09,849 --> 00:19:14,120
Boss, starting today, I'll do anything—
begging, stealing, whatever it takes!

266
00:19:14,774 --> 00:19:17,960
All right, good attitude. 
Go make us some real money.

267
00:19:18,040 --> 00:19:18,467
Yes.

268
00:19:19,132 --> 00:19:20,112
That's strange.

269
00:19:20,520 --> 00:19:21,960
Don't worry about it.

270
00:19:27,389 --> 00:19:30,200
Mokku, just like you said, 
I brought my friends!

271
00:19:30,524 --> 00:19:32,540
Thank you. Now listen, everyone.

272
00:19:33,559 --> 00:19:38,039
From now on, if you do anything bad at all,
this crow will peck your butts.

273
00:19:38,629 --> 00:19:41,620
But if we don't bring in any money, 
the boss will whip us!

274
00:19:41,979 --> 00:19:44,122
I'll take the beatings for you.

275
00:19:44,146 --> 00:19:46,736
I'm made of oak, 
so it doesn't hurt me at all.

276
00:19:48,180 --> 00:19:52,155
No way! The boss is way too scary!

277
00:19:54,281 --> 00:19:57,200
Aaargh! Ow, ow, ow!!

278
00:19:57,201 --> 00:19:58,760
It hurts...

279
00:20:00,987 --> 00:20:03,080
Ow, ow, ow, ow!!

280
00:20:03,081 --> 00:20:04,920
Ow!! All right, stop!

281
00:20:05,259 --> 00:20:07,060
Good, that should be enough!

282
00:20:09,214 --> 00:20:10,720
Got that, everyone?!

283
00:20:15,199 --> 00:20:17,940
What do you mean you
didn't bring in any money?!

284
00:20:18,669 --> 00:20:20,360
You lazy bums!!

285
00:20:20,509 --> 00:20:23,632
I'm the one who took everyone away. 
Beat only m—

286
00:20:23,992 --> 00:20:24,960
- Ow!
- You bastard!

287
00:20:25,717 --> 00:20:26,780
You bastard!

288
00:20:28,722 --> 00:20:29,940
Ow!

289
00:20:29,941 --> 00:20:30,520
Ow!

290
00:20:30,660 --> 00:20:33,360
- Take that! 
- Ow!

291
00:20:33,685 --> 00:20:34,685
Ow!

292
00:20:35,159 --> 00:20:36,180
Ow!

293
00:20:38,559 --> 00:20:40,880
Starting tomorrow, you better do whatever 
dirty work it takes to bring in cash!

294
00:20:40,990 --> 00:20:43,708
Steal, pick pockets, do whatever it takes!

295
00:20:58,114 --> 00:21:02,505
You damn fool! How many days has it 
been since you brought in any money?!

296
00:21:03,116 --> 00:21:06,460
Ow! It hurts! Ow!

297
00:21:22,179 --> 00:21:24,120
They must be wearing down by now.

298
00:21:24,144 --> 00:21:25,640
Yeah, time to make our move.

299
00:21:26,747 --> 00:21:31,471
I've whipped you over ten times today, 
yet you didn't earn a thing!

300
00:21:31,495 --> 00:21:35,112
If you want good food and booze, 
you should work for it yourself!

301
00:21:35,869 --> 00:21:38,205
What did you say?! Say that again!

302
00:21:38,229 --> 00:21:41,521
If you're starving because you 
won't work, it's your own fault!

303
00:21:42,186 --> 00:21:44,120
W-Why, you little...!

304
00:21:48,660 --> 00:21:49,660
Now!

305
00:21:52,698 --> 00:21:53,769
Take that!

306
00:21:54,960 --> 00:21:56,300
The magic ring!

307
00:21:56,380 --> 00:21:57,739
Crow, wait!

308
00:21:57,780 --> 00:21:59,137
Give back the ring!

309
00:21:59,245 --> 00:22:00,347
Hey, wait!

310
00:22:01,700 --> 00:22:04,846
Without that ring, the spell will break!

311
00:22:04,900 --> 00:22:06,737
It worked! Now then!

312
00:22:20,206 --> 00:22:21,090
Mokku.

313
00:22:21,919 --> 00:22:26,760
Grandpa, those puppets were only 
moving because of magic, weren't they?

314
00:22:27,360 --> 00:22:33,920
When I made you, I poured all my 
love into it. Magic alone isn't enough.

315
00:22:45,014 --> 00:22:46,971
Spare some change, please...

316
00:22:46,995 --> 00:22:51,409
People who try to take the easy way out
without working always end up like that.

317
00:22:51,433 --> 00:22:53,940
Yeah, starting tomorrow, I'll work too.

318
00:22:54,554 --> 00:22:56,240
That's the spirit.

319
00:22:56,445 --> 00:22:57,524
Grandpa?

320
00:22:58,478 --> 00:23:00,014
I'm tired.

321
00:23:00,100 --> 00:23:02,424
Didn't you just say you were going to work?

322
00:23:02,448 --> 00:23:05,600
But my legs are completely worn out, 
I really can't move!

323
00:23:05,820 --> 00:23:06,623
Carry me on your back.

324
00:23:06,699 --> 00:23:07,999
What am I going to do with you...

325
00:23:08,185 --> 00:23:08,833
All right.

326
00:23:13,199 --> 00:23:15,900
Kind sirs to my left and right...

327
00:23:16,664 --> 00:23:21,080
Please spare some charity, 
have pity on a poor...

328
00:23:33,229 --> 00:23:36,036
<i>Mokku runs around shouting at the top
of his lungs for the whole town to hear.</i>

329
00:23:36,849 --> 00:23:39,264
<i>Mokku frightens everyone 
with endless lies...</i>

330
00:23:39,288 --> 00:23:42,440
<i>...claiming there is a monster in the 
forest or that a house is on fire.</i>

331
00:23:43,629 --> 00:23:48,620
<i>To punish Mokku, the Oak Tree Fairy makes
his nose grow longer and longer.</i>

332
00:23:49,600 --> 00:23:53,851
<i>Desperate to get his nose back to normal,
Mokku promises to be a good boy...</i>

333
00:23:53,875 --> 00:23:57,120
<i>...but will he be able to keep 
that promise to the very end?</i>

334
00:23:57,646 --> 00:24:00,126
<i>Look forward to next week's 
Kashi no Ki Mokku!</i>

